Measurement 0006's own section F names ~12 reports against "the measurement's
own packet builder, NOT hypergumbo" and ends "Fix before reuse." The builder
was a session artifact and was never committed, so its defects could only be
re-encountered rather than fixed -- the same failure WI-ratuv recorded when an
uncommitted script made a 589 -> 782 delta unattributable. This puts it in the
repo as `measure-taint-precision.py packet`, with 42 tests, one per defect.

THE LOAD-BEARING DEFECT. The builder searched for sink sites only inside the
SOURCE symbol's span. ArkLib#3's path is main (201-255) then generate_dot_graph
(110-137), and `open` is called in the SECOND, so the packet printed
"(none found in span)" for a sink plainly present two symbols along. Measured
on 0006's own shipped packets:

    packets2/ (the 112 adjudicated situations)   66 EMPTY sink listings (58.9%)

For nearly six adjudications in ten the reader applying 0001's rubric was shown
manufactured absence. Both directions of error follow from that, and every
published 0006 figure -- 33.9% correctness, 24.1% useful -- rests on those 112
adjudications. Searching every first-party symbol on the flow's path takes the
empty rate to 0.3%. DENOMINATORS DIFFER (112 sampled vs 730 all-collected) and
that is disclosed rather than smoothed over; the mechanism is not in doubt.

THE OTHER THREE NAMED DEFECTS, closed with it:
  - substring matching (`format` matched inside `information`; `-> ` inside a
    quoted pattern matched the bash redirect `>`) -> identifier-boundary
    matching, plus length-preserving comment and string scrubbing;
  - `$VAR` matched in comments and locals -> shell expansions matched outside
    comments, with locally-bound names excluded;
  - missed literal call sites -> every primitive a COLLAPSED situation stands
    for is searched, not just the headline sink_name. ArkLib#3 collapses open,
    file.write and json.dump; only `open` was searched.
An honest empty now NAMES WHAT WAS SEARCHED, so a reader can tell "not there"
from "not looked for" -- the distinction whose absence made the original
listing misleading rather than merely thin.

TWO DEFECTS IN MY OWN FIX, FOUND BY READING RENDERED PACKETS BACK AGAINST
SOURCE, neither caught by the unit fixtures (which all used function-kind
symbols, where the declared span is right):
  (a) a FILE-anchored symbol declares span 1-1 --
      bash:scripts/lintWhitespace.sh:1-1:file:file for a 26-line script -- so
      honouring it searched ONE line and reported "none found" for a redirect
      on line 10. Defect 4 arriving by another route. File symbols are now
      searched whole, and the header reports the EFFECTIVE span so a hit on
      line 16 cannot sit under a heading saying 1-1.
  (b) shell locals bound by `read -r file` / `for f in` were listed as
      environment reads, because only `NAME=` was excluded. That ArkLib
      situation listed `$file` on four lines as an env_read source; with both
      fixes it reports NO environment read anywhere in the file, which points
      the adjudication the OPPOSITE way from what the old packet supported.

RESIDUAL, STATED NOT HIDDEN: block comments are not handled (a regex over 16
languages would trade a known limitation for an unknown one), and shell
assignment detection has no notion of order or scope, so a name both inherited
AND reassigned reads as local and is dropped. Both err toward showing the
adjudicator LESS, which is the safe direction for a listing whose job is to
support a refutation.

